cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Syntonic Engine"
abstract: >-
  A joint correction loop whose time window comes from the Syntony Principle (Theorem U'), with nothing tuned.
  Implemented in Python, C++ and Rust, which agree to about 1e-14 rad. On the simulated MAESTRO 1 joint bench it
  matches a joint-by-joint tuned PID at the baton tip under steady noise and does better when the noise jumps.
